<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)) || \old(this.get(i)) == null);</code>
--------------------
To generate the appropriate assert statement for the given comment, we need to ensure that for every index from 0 up to, but not including, the specified index, the element at that position remains unchanged from its previous state, unless it was initially null.

Here's how we can express this in an assert statement:

1. We need to compare the elements at each index before and after the `set` operation.
2. We need to ensure that the comparison only happens for indices less than the specified index.
3. We need to account for the possibility that an element might have been initially null.

Given these points, the assert statement can be written as follows:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)) || \old(this.get(i)) == null);</code>

This assert statement checks that for every index `i` from 0 to `index-1`, the element at that index either remains the same or was initially null.
