Here's how we can express this in an assert statement:

1. We need to check that for every index `i` from 0 to `index - 1`, the element at position `i` remains the same as it was before the `set` operation, unless it was initially null.
2. We can use the `\old` syntax to refer to the value of the element at position `i` before the `set` operation.
3. We can use the `\forall` quantifier to express that the condition must hold for all indices `i` in the specified range.

The resulting assert statement would be:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (\old(this.get(i)) == null || this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)));</code>

This ensures that for every index `i` from 0 to `index - 1`, the element at position `i` either remains the same or was initially null.
